cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PruneStack: performance-diversity ensemble pruning with nested evaluation"
type: software
version: 2.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mITz85/prunestack-py"
abstract: >-
  PruneStack selects subsets of a heterogeneous pool of 120 base models with a
  bi-objective fitness alpha*P + (1 - alpha)*D searched by Elephant Herding
  Optimization, evaluates vote and stacking combiners inside a nested
  cross-validation protocol, and extracts dataset and pool meta-features. The
  paper/ folder contains the per-dataset results and the analysis scripts of
  the accompanying manuscript.
authors:
  - family-names: Domladovac
    given-names: Marko
    email: marko@mitz-is.me
    affiliation: "University of Zagreb, Faculty of Organization and Informatics, Varaždin, Croatia"
keywords:
  - ensemble pruning
  - stacking
  - diversity
  - meta-learning
  - elephant herding optimization
  - nested cross-validation
